From: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: only the security-control clock ahead of the config writes

0912 enabled all package clocks before the work mode write. That does
not work: nss_cc_apb_bridge_clk runs from the switch core source, which
is fed by the QCA8084 SerDes clock, and the SerDes is only set up later
in the same function. The enable fails with "status stuck at 'off'",
config_init returns -EBUSY and the PPE driver never probes (BE7000 test
build uniphy9: no Ethernet at all).

Keep the original order and turn on just nss_cc_sec_ctrl_ahb_clk, which
runs from the AHB source that the critical AHB branches already keep
up, before the WORK_MODE_CFG and EPHY_CFG writes; the package clock
init at the end stays as it was.

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
index c766173..3601bfd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -1130,11 +1130,14 @@ static int qca8084_phy_package_config_init_once(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	/* The work mode and EPHY_CFG registers below sit in the security
 	 * control block, clocked by nss_cc_sec_ctrl_ahb_clk. Nothing holds
 	 * that clock before this point, so clk_disable_unused() has gated it
-	 * by the time we get here and the writes are dropped: on a failing
+	 * by the time we get here and the writes were dropped: on a failing
 	 * BE7000 the work mode still read the reset default (0x3f, switch
-	 * bit set) long after this ran. Enable the package clocks first.
+	 * bit set) long after this ran. Only this clock is turned on early:
+	 * it runs from the AHB source that is already up, while the rest of
+	 * the package clocks (APB bridge, switch core) hang off the SerDes
+	 * clock and cannot be enabled before the SerDes is set up below.
 	 */
-	ret = qca8084_package_clock_init(shared_priv);
+	ret = clk_prepare_enable(shared_priv->clk[SEC_CTRL_AHB_CLK]);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -1194,7 +1197,10 @@ static int qca8084_phy_package_config_init_once(struct phy_device *phydev)
 			phydev_info(phydev, "QXGMII XPCS set up without BaseR lock, will redo it on first link up\n");
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	/* Initialize the PHY package clock and reset, which is the
+	 * necessary config sequence after GPIO reset on the PHY package.
+	 */
+	return qca8084_package_clock_init(shared_priv);
 }
 
 static int qca8084_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
